{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convective heat transfer coefficient convective heat transfer coefficient","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md","fileName":"Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conduction Convection and Radiation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"convective heat transfer coefficient convective heat transfer coefficient","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md","fileName":"Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient","heading":"Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Newton's law of cooling expresses convective heat rate as $q=Ah(T_s-T_\\infty)$. The coefficient $h$ packages the effect of fluid velocity, orientation, surface condition, and other flow characteristics on exchange between a wall and the surrounding bulk fluid.\n\nBecause $h$ represents a coupled transport process, it is not generally a fixed material property. Correlations or experiments supply an effective value, and [[Thermal Model Verification and Sensitivity|sensitivity analysis]] should test its influence when flow conditions